  "debrief": "The route isn’t found by the browser, but by the routers along the way. They use the same idea as you: they look for the smallest total. This method is called Dijkstra’s algorithm. And that’s why big websites put copies of their files on servers close to people (CDN): the fastest cable across the ocean is the one you never have to use."
